## 7. Binary Search with Comparison Count

```python id="rq9mv5"
nums = list(map(int, input("Enter sorted numbers: ").split()))
key = int(input("Enter search key: "))

low = 0
high = len(nums) - 1
count = 0

while low <= high:
    mid = (low + high) // 2
    count += 1

    if nums[mid] == key:
        print("Element found at position", mid + 1)
        print("Comparisons =", count)
        break
    elif nums[mid] < key:
        low = mid + 1
    else:
        high = mid - 1
else:
    print("Element not found")
```
